    {
      "id": "cmip6-mlotst-definition",
      "severity": "must",
      "path": "concepts/cmip6-mlotst-definition.md",
      "sha256": "7c9f821afb300a640b26dbd03993d309a09793518640191dc82d641f6a4f5cb5",
      "reason": "It gives the sigma-t/buoyancy criterion, local-pressure evaluation, and online-then-monthly-averaging construction of mlotst that the offline operator MLD must reproduce.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "Apply the `mlotst` criterion exactly: displaced-parcel δB > ΔB_crit = 0.0003 m s-2 (≈ Δρ_crit = 0.03 kg m-3), crossing depth linearly interpolated between the bracketing levels, referenced to the model's shallowest level; pass that as `ref_depth` to `compute_mixed_layer_depth` because `mlotst` is referenced to the ocean surface, not 10 m.",
        "State the three residual causes — reference level, displaced-parcel-at-local-pressure vs σ0 density form, and instantaneous-MLD averaging vs MLD of monthly means (offline MLD expected shallower) — and do not report them as model error; drop columns where the threshold is never reached (GFDL/MPI fill ~full column depth, CESM2 often 0 m) and report the excluded area; note GFDL-ESM4's native 75 hybrid layers were remapped to 35 z levels."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "monthly-means-are-time-averages",
      "severity": "must",
      "path": "pitfalls/monthly-means-are-time-averages.md",
      "sha256": "df6b5c23460f88f1522e5c6a665e1efbb8322c3ae876c885530f3019aa284ee0",
      "reason": "The offline MLD is a nonlinear diagnostic computed from monthly mean thetao/so, so it will differ from the monthly mean of the online MLD stored as mlotst, which is central to interpreting the disagreement.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "Compute the MLD of each monthly profile and then average the monthly MLDs; never average `thetao`/`so` first — state that the diagnostic-first order was used, since f(monthly mean) ≠ mean of f.",
        "Each March/September climatology is the plain mean of that month's values across the 30 years (no day weights); day weighting via `temporal_aggregate` applies only to means spanning different calendar months."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "common-comparison-mask",
      "severity": "must",
      "path": "methods/common-comparison-mask.md",
      "sha256": "bbb98200f52b4a692ce097704b8c438179a795a44bec6b856c03cf31931af4ea",
      "reason": "The mean difference, RMSE, correlation and ranking must be computed only where both operator MLD and mlotst are defined, using one common mask over the fields being compared.",
      "status": "summary_fallback",
      "fallback": "the notes failed the check",
      "violations": [
        "`here` is not in the selected fragments or the question"
      ],
      "rejected_notes": [
        "Build one mask over operator MLD and `mlotst` together with `build_comparison_mask` and apply `.where(mask)` to both before bias, RMSE and correlation, so all three statistics come from one sample; report the recorded cell counts.",
        "Pass `ocean_only=False`: WOA23 is not part of this comparison, so the default would silently import WOA23's coastline; report `mean_data`/`mean_reference` from `compute_difference_metrics` with the bias."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "cmip6-thetao-potential-temperature",
      "severity": "should",
      "path": "concepts/cmip6-thetao-potential-temperature.md",
      "sha256": "cf8b1424a04be2e18362300d2e76d09e3f958f9d6a451c733a0cf9938968e73c",
      "reason": "thetao is potential temperature in every CMIP6 model, which matters for the density calculation used to derive the operator MLD.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "`thetao` is potential temperature (no `bigthetao` exists locally), so density/MLD must go through the potential-temperature route read by `temperature_kind()` in `src/tools/scientific_calculator.py`; the in-situ route biases density increasingly with depth."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "cmip6-so-practical-salinity",
      "severity": "should",
      "path": "concepts/cmip6-so-practical-salinity.md",
      "sha256": "96f2763290996040d675ca6e8f997ea29fa320b8f6e6793bf2c6fcb739345e19",
      "reason": "CMIP6 so is practical salinity, so deriving Absolute Salinity for the density criterion requires treating it accordingly.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "`so` is practical salinity with units \"0.001\" and stored values ~35 — no ×0.001 or ×1000; before TEOS-10 (gsw) density calls convert S_P to S_A with the location-dependent function, otherwise the MLD bias varies by region."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "cmip6-static-grid-fields",
      "severity": "should",
      "path": "concepts/cmip6-static-grid-fields.md",
      "sha256": "2ad0548ca0993fa57d8f1fad27a267dcf9c0e1d007a74343d4bbdbf5b4f1ca17",
      "reason": "areacello is the tracer-cell horizontal area needed for area-weighted percentages and for relating the comparison cells to each model's total ocean area.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "Take cell thickness as `volcello` / `areacello` (`cell_thickness_like` in `src/tools/data_loader.py`), not `lev_bnds` differences, which fail at partial top/bottom cells (GFDL-ESM4 differs >1 % in 14 % of cells; GFDL `volcello` is monthly).",
        "Total ocean area differs between models by about a per cent; state the model's own `areacello` total each percentage is taken over rather than rescaling one model to another."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "cmip6-grid-labels",
      "severity": "should",
      "path": "datasets/cmip6-grid-labels.md",
      "sha256": "e349f9e305621b6c10b35cccd0490da521cc7e3ba08bfb53890479f81024d117",
      "reason": "The distinction between native curvilinear grids and GFDL-ESM4's regridded output affects masks, which operations are exact, and the display-only regridding required for Figure 1.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "GFDL-ESM4 is `gr`: its values and mask are already remapped to 1° (conserve_order1), so its comparison is on the archive grid, not the native one.",
        "CESM2 (100 km) vs MPI (250 km) resolution differs ~2.5×; features narrower than the coarse grid are not comparable in amplitude, so say so where disagreement concentrates."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "missing-values-and-land-cells",
